+Actual epistemic achievement requires relevant relations of formation and correction. Its ethical place also depends on what comes to live, relate and develop. Living significance gives every living claim significance, and the direction of 生生 (read separately, D1) gives life and further generation a positive place, without requiring an exclusive inventory of all values. Thus a pluralist may be compatible, while a strict experiential-value account identifies a substantive possible conflict beyond its accepted scope. The whole helping relationship preserves changes in both lives even when both benefit overall. These refinements sharpen the wider argument without proving universal semantic sufficiency, consciousness or whole-theory necessity.
 
